From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:30:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] U12 review: hermetic year-map in the gate test, stricter
 dash rule, year labels

- server/family-gate.test.ts: seeded scenarios no longer read the repo's
  generated year map, so the rename scenario passes once U10's
  familyYear.generated.ts is in the tree (the wave 1 integration seam).
- validate-family.mjs: any "--" in family prose fails (the old pattern
  missed "word-- word" and "word --word"); a catechism count is read only
  in copy that points at the family catechism, so a glossary page giving
  the Westminster or Heidelberg count cannot fail the gate.
- The 72 weekly devotions were still called "a year" in the devotions
  page's SEO title and description, the catalogue summary, and the
  Resources note ("A devotion for every week of the year"). Each now says
  seventy-two, more than a year, and the gate checks the number.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
